{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014VqLL4z4eB84GnVW3KcuLS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0161FKUf51BUujVMvKKkJjmM","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/structfuse-context/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260512T204322/best/paper.tex","limit":30},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4016,"cache_read_input_tokens":53621,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4016,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0146hp8VT5paWxaM372yiqKN","session_id":"163407e6-eb14-494f-b2b9-ca41e03f7d7e","uuid":"f6e23971-ac16-4403-ad3a-34ba8b29a65b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0161FKUf51BUujVMvKKkJjmM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n2\t\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n3\t\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n4\t\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,amsfonts}\n5\t\\usepackage{booktabs}\n6\t\\usepackage{multirow}\n7\t\\usepackage{graphicx}\n8\t\\usepackage{hyperref}\n9\t\\usepackage{xcolor}\n10\t\\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}\n11\t\\usepackage{natbib}\n12\t\\usepackage{tabularx}\n13\t\\usepackage{enumitem}\n14\t\n15\t\\title{StructFuse: Structure-Grounded Hard Negative Mining\\\\for Contrastive Code Context Retrieval}\n16\t\n17\t\\author{\n18\t  Anonymous Authors\n19\t}\n20\t\n21\t\\date{}\n22\t\n23\t\\begin{document}\n24\t\\maketitle\n25\t\n26\t% ============================================================\n27\t\\begin{abstract}\n28\tRepo-level code repair requires retrieving relevant files from large codebases, yet current retrievers conflate lexical similarity with structural relevance.\n29\tWe introduce \\textsc{StructFuse}, a contrastive training framework that mines \\emph{structure-grounded hard negatives}---files that are lexically similar to the query but structurally disconnected according to inter-procedural data-flow analysis.\n30\tUsing scope-bounded CodeQL analysis over 5{,}000 repositories, we extract call-graph and data-flow connectivity and identify that 42.1\\% of instances contain files that are structurally connected to the bug locus but absent from the gold patch, providing a rich source of contrastive signal."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0146hp8VT5paWxaM372yiqKN","session_id":"163407e6-eb14-494f-b2b9-ca41e03f7d7e","uuid":"a4def9fc-e399-4532-b775-89046d498860","timestamp":"2026-05-16T16:17:25.223Z"}
